  "body": "LOCAL PLANNING WORKSPACE / 01\nTraining draft\n\nFour practice sessions. Explicit constraints. A draft you can inspect.\n\nSynthetic practice only — not an issued schedule.\n1. Prepare the requests\n\nMinutes from Day 1 minute 0. Day 2 starts at 1440. People, rooms and required qualifications stay fixed.\n\n4 requests retained: A, B, C, D\n\nSession A\nP01 | Room-1 | Q-A\nDuration (minutes)\nAllowed starts (minutes)\nSession B\nP01 | Room-1 | Q-A\nDuration (minutes)\nAllowed starts (minutes)\nSession C\nP02 | Room-2 | Q-B\nDuration (minutes)\nAllowed starts (minutes)\nSession D\nP02 | Room-2 | Q-B\nDuration (minutes)\nAllowed starts (minutes)\n2. Check the supplied rules\nOperating windows\nWindow format: 0-240;1440-1680. Entire sessions must fit.\nP01 · whole-horizon limits\nSupplied qualifications\nAvailability windows\nMaximum minutes, both days\nMinimum rest (minutes)\nP02 · whole-horizon limits\nSupplied qualifications\nAvailability windows\nMaximum minutes, both days\nMinimum rest (minutes)\nEvaluator settings\nSearch allowance (candidate attempts)\n1–200000 nodes. A stopped search cannot prove infeasibility.\n3. Inspect the draft\nGenerate draft\n\nFeasible draft — all 4 requests scheduled.\n\nA | 120–180 | P01 | Room-1\nB | 30–90 | P01 | Room-1\nC | 0–60 | P02 | Room-2\nD | 1440–1500 | P02 | Room-2\nP01: 120 / 120 minutes across both days\nP02: 120 / 120 minutes across both days\n\nFeasibility covers supplied starts and constraints only. Intervals are half-open; rest is checked separately. Budgets cover both days combined.\n\nMark current draft reviewed\n\nNot reviewed — current inputs need review.\n\nInspect every assignment and both personnel totals, then mark reviewed.\n4. Save and recover\n\nLocal browser storage and portable synthetic JSON. No account or remote storage.\n\nSave portable draft\n\nUnsaved changes — save a new portable checkpoint.\n\nImport snapshot file (.json)\nOr paste snapshot JSON\nCheck import\n\nCurrent work stays in place until you confirm replacement.\n\nRead limitations\nSynthetic-only prototype · Offline calculation · No operational integrations",
